--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -1,11 +1,152 @@
 Noteworthy changes in release a.b
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
-* New environment variable HTS_GCS_HOST, analogous to the existing
-  HTS_S3_HOST, to redirect gs:// URLs to a caller-specified endpoint
-  (e.g. a local GCS emulator such as fake-gcs-server) using path-style
-  addressing instead of the normal BUCKET.storage.googleapis.com
-  virtual-hosted-style addressing.
+* NEW. Added environment variable HTS_GCS_HOST, analogous to the existing
+  HTS_S3_HOST, to redirect gs:// URLs to a caller-specified endpoint.
+  (PR #2051.  Thanks to Peter Dowdy)
+
+Updates
+-------
+
+* Various code quality improvements.  Added memory and error
+  checks.  Some changes to better data types.
+  (PR #2054, PR #2059, PR #2064, PR #2066, PR #2070, PR #2073, PR #2075,
+   PR #2077, PR #2078)
+
+* Add a new format option to strip UR tags from CRAM.
+  (PR #2056, partial fix for samtools/samtools#2327.  Requested by
+   Florian Plaza Oñate)
+
+* Report when khash can no longer expand.
+  (PR #2063)
+
+* Use multi iterators in the synced reader.  This adds bcf_itr_regions() and
+  tbx_itr_regions() interfaces as BCF and tabix equivalents to
+  sam_itr_regions().  This can speed up `bcftools view`.
+  (PR #2052, fixes samtools/bcftools#2557. Reported by Carsten Erickson)
+
+* Apply CURL_CA_BUNDLE environment variable in the S3 backend.
+  (PR #2069.  Thanks to John Marshall)
+
+* Cram embed_ref=2 and huffman optimisation.
+  (PR #2082)
+
+* API fix. Protect against out of bounds ref id in cram_put_bam_seq.
+  (PR #2087)
+
+* Adds validation to options specified using hts_opt_add or cram_set_voption.
+  Mostly for overflow detection.
+  (PR #2095. Reported by Sn0wyDay)
+
+* Return an error instead of calling abort in hts_getline().
+  (PR #2093, fixes #2091.  Reported by an)
+
+* bcf_set_variant_type() now recognises single break-ends as described
+  in section 5.4.9 of the VCF 4.5 specification.
+  (PR #2115, fixes #2108)
+
+Build Changes
+-------------
+
+* Add more CI tests for a variety of Linux and non-Linux platforms.
+  (PR #2053)
+
+* Update build badge, remove .cirrus.yml, spelling corrections.
+  (PR #2071.  Thanks to John Marshall)
+
+* Make check_copyright.pl better at skipping auto-generated files.
+  (PR #2080)
+
+* Use bash and pipefail for tests using simple_test_driver.sh
+  (PR #2083)
+
+* Add S3 integration tests.
+  (PR #2067.  Thanks to Peter Dowdy)
+
+Bug fixes
+---------
+
+* Fix an undefined behaviour in os/rand.c
+  (PR #2050)
+
+* Fix heapsort bug and add ksort tests and improved documentation in comments.
+  (PR #2055)
+
+* Fix possible leak of bgzidx_t::offs and changes to bgzidx_t::noffs and
+  bgzidx_t::moffs data types.
+  (PR #2057)
+
+* Remove an assert in cram_index_build and have it fail more gracefully.
+  (PR #2061, fixes #2060.  Reported and co-authored by Shujie Xiang)
+
+* Remove an infinite loop in bam_mods_at_qpos().
+  (PR #2068)
+
+* Avoid calling libcurl functions if curl_global_init() failed.
+  (Part of PR #2069.  Thanks to John Marshall)
+
+* Make sam_format_aux1 'A' type be nul terminated.
+  (PR #2079)
+
+* Fix multiple VCF header parsing bugs.
+  (PR #2074, fixes #2065  Reported by Mark Woon)
+
+* Prevent integer overflow in resolve_cigar2().
+  (PR #2072)
+
+* Improved code testing with the addition of a fuzzer for the expression
+  filters (hts_expr).  This resulted in the detection and correction of several
+  serious expression parsing bugs.
+  (PR #2076)
+
+* Fix leak of region list in hts_itr_multi_bam().
+  (PR #2084)
+
+* Improve checking of SEQ/CIGAR consistency when processing records with CG
+  tags.
+  (PR # 2089. Fixes oss-fuzz issue  560967311)
+
+* Stop the CRAM zlib decoder from getting stuck in an endless loop.
+  (PR #2085, fixes #2081.  Reported by Sewon Ahn)
+
+* Fix hts_set_filter_expression(fp, NULL) so that it properly disables filtering
+  without leaving a dangling pointer.
+  (PR #2094.  Reported and code fix suggestion by Sewon Ahn)
+
+* Tighten version number limits in bcf_get_version()
+  (PR #2092, fixes #2088. Reported by an)
+
+* Fix CRAM query of unaligned ('*') reads.
+  (PR #2100, fixes samtools/samtools#2396.  Reported by Matt Sexton)
+
+* Fix hfile_s3 reads failing at EOF on a part boundary.
+  (PR #2098, fixes #2097.  Thanks to Peter Dowdy)
+
+* Reduce CRAM decode memory usage when multi-threading.  Previous improvements
+  to threaded throughput added greater memory usage, especially with long reads.
+  This change mitigates that.
+  (PR #2102, fixes samtools/samtools#2393.  Reported by Matthieu Muffato)
+
+* Prevent negative range start in multi-region iterators, which could in
+  some cases cause the index look-up to become stuck in an endless loop.
+  (PR #2110.  Reported by haehet)
+
+* Fix SQ line removal using sam_hdr_remove_lines().  It failed to update
+  some internal sam_hdr_t structures, leading to deleted SQ lines reappearing,
+  notably when writing BAM files.
+  (PR #2105)
+
+* Fix the wildly incorrect length value returned by hfile_mem_get_buffer()
+  and hfile_mem_steal_buffer().
+  (PR #2109)
+
+* Fix a number of bugs that could be triggered by removing all samples
+  with bcf_hdr_set_samples().
+  (PR #2114)
+
+* Fix fai_load3() crash if a .fai index was present but it attempted
+  a rebuild because it also needed a .gzi one, and the rebuild failed.
+  (PR #2116)
 
 Noteworthy changes in release 1.24 (9th July 2026)
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
